---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '@components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '@components/Footer.astro';

const effectiveDate = 'May 12, 2026';
---

<Layout
	title='Privacy Policy | Design2Tailwind'
	description='How Design2Tailwind (operated by Red Pixel LLC) collects, uses, and protects your information when you visit our website or engage our services.'>
	<Header />

	<div class='container flex flex-col pt-36 mb-20 lg:pt-44 lg:flex-row xl:pt-52'>
		<div class='mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl'>
			<h1 class='font-Recoleta font-normal text-black text-3xl! lg:text-4xl! xl:text-[43px]/[48px]! mt-8'>
				Privacy Policy
			</h1>
			<p class='text-black/60 font-body text-sm md:text-base mt-3'>
				Effective {effectiveDate}
			</p>

			<div
				class='prose-blog prose relative mt-8 max-w-none prose-headings:mt-8 prose-headings:font-Recoleta prose-headings:font-normal prose-li:marker:text-black text-black font-Gordita md:prose-lg prose-h2:!text-3xl prose-h3:!text-2xl'>
				<p>
					Design2Tailwind ("we," "us," or "our") is a service operated by Red Pixel LLC, a Delaware limited
					liability company. This Privacy Policy explains what information we collect when you visit
					<a href='https://design2tailwind.com'>design2tailwind.com</a> or engage us for design-to-code services,
					how we use it, and the choices you have.
				</p>

				<h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>

				<h3>1.1 Information you provide directly</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>Quote and contact requests.</strong> When you use our "Get a Free Quote" form or email us at
						<a href='mailto:hello@design2tailwind.com'>hello@design2tailwind.com</a>, we receive the name, email
						address, company, project description, and any files or links you share so we can respond.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Newsletter and RSS.</strong> If you subscribe to our newsletter, we collect your email address.
						RSS feed access does not require any personal information.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Client engagement information.</strong> If we enter into a services agreement with you, we
						collect billing details, project assets (designs, brand materials, copy), and any access credentials
						you choose to share for delivery.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h3>1.2 Information collected automatically</h3>
				<ul>
					<li>
						<strong>Analytics.</strong> We use <a href='https://usefathom.com' rel='noopener'>Fathom Analytics</a>,
						a privacy-focused analytics service that does not use cookies, does not collect personal data, and is
						GDPR/PECR/CCPA-compliant by default. Fathom records anonymized, aggregated information such as page
						views, referrers, country, and device type.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Strictly necessary cookies.</strong> Our site is delivered through Cloudflare, which may set
						short-lived security and performance cookies (for example, <code>__cf_bm</code>) to protect against
						abuse. We do not use third-party advertising or tracking cookies.
					</li>
					<li>
						<strong>Server logs.</strong> Our hosting provider may temporarily log IP addresses and request
						metadata for security and reliability purposes.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>2. How We Use Your Information</h2>
				<p>We use the information described above to:</p>
				<ul>
					<li>Respond to quote requests, inquiries, and support questions.</li>
					<li>Deliver and invoice agreed-upon design-to-code services.</li>
					<li>Send newsletter content you have subscribed to.</li>
					<li>Understand aggregate site traffic and improve content and pages.</li>
					<li>Protect our website and clients from fraud, abuse, and security threats.</li>
					<li>Comply with applicable legal obligations.</li>
				</ul>

				<h2>3. How We Share Your Information</h2>
				<p>
					We do not sell your personal information. We share information only with service providers that help us
					operate the business under appropriate confidentiality terms. Current providers include:
				</p>
				<ul>
					<li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> &mdash; hosting and CDN for design2tailwind.com.</li>
					<li><strong>Fathom Analytics</strong> &mdash; anonymized website analytics.</li>
					<li><strong>Email and invoicing providers</strong> &mdash; to send quotes, newsletters, and invoices.</li>
				</ul>
				<p>
					We may also disclose information if required by law, to enforce our agreements, or to protect the rights,
					property, or safety of Red Pixel LLC, our clients, or others.
				</p>

				<h2>4. Data Retention</h2>
				<p>
					We retain information for as long as needed to provide the services or as required for legal,
					accounting, or reporting purposes. Quote inquiries that do not become engagements are retained for up to
					24 months and then deleted or anonymized. Engagement records are retained for the duration of the
					project plus the period required by applicable tax and contract law.
				</p>

				<h2>5. Your Rights and Choices</h2>
				<p>
					Depending on where you live, you may have rights under laws such as the GDPR (EU/UK) or CCPA
					(California) to access, correct, delete, or port your personal information, and to object to or restrict
					certain processing. To exercise any of these rights, email us at
					<a href='mailto:hello@design2tailwind.com'>hello@design2tailwind.com</a>. We will respond within the
					timeframe required by applicable law.
				</p>
				<p>
					You can unsubscribe from our newsletter at any time using the link in any newsletter email. Because we
					use Fathom Analytics, no opt-out is necessary for analytics &mdash; we do not track you personally.
				</p>

				<h2>6. International Transfers</h2>
				<p>
					Red Pixel LLC is based in the United States. If you access our website or services from outside the
					United States, your information may be processed in the United States or other countries where our
					service providers operate. We rely on appropriate safeguards (such as standard contractual clauses)
					where required.
				</p>

				<h2>7. Security</h2>
				<p>
					We use commercially reasonable administrative, technical, and physical safeguards to protect the
					information we collect. No system is perfectly secure, however, and we cannot guarantee the absolute
					security of information transmitted to us over the internet.
				</p>

				<h2>8. Children</h2>
				<p>
					Our website and services are intended for businesses and adults. We do not knowingly collect personal
					information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided us information, please contact
					us and we will delete it.
				</p>

				<h2>9. Changes to This Policy</h2>
				<p>
					We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will revise the "Effective" date at
					the top of this page. Material changes will be highlighted on this page for at least 30 days.
				</p>

				<h2>10. Contact Us</h2>
				<p>
					For privacy questions or requests, email
					<a href='mailto:hello@design2tailwind.com'>hello@design2tailwind.com</a>.
				</p>
				<p>
					Red Pixel LLC<br />
					Operating as Design2Tailwind<br />
					Delaware, United States
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>

	<Footer />
</Layout>
